___________________________________________________________________________ INTRODUCTION
The Rise of Big Data in Marketing
In the contemporary digital era, the proliferation of big data has emerged as a transformative force in the realm of marketing. The advent of big data analytics has enabled businesses to access a wealth of information about their clients, encompassing demographics, social media
activity, and purchasing habits. This abundance of data has given rise to sophisticated analytical tools and techniques, fundamentally altering the way businesses approach market segmentation, targeting, and personalized marketing strategies. The concept of big data transcends traditional data analysis, as it involves the processing of vast
and complex datasets that are beyond the capability of conventional software tools. This paradigm shift is not confined to retail marketing analytics but is broadly relevant to contemporary corporate strategies across various sectors (Weinman, 2018). The strategic applications of big data encompass four key digital disciplines: information excellence, solution
leadership, collective intimacy, and accelerated innovation. These disciplines collectively enhance customer value, galvanize corporate strategy, and link information technologies to business success. In the context of marketing, big data analytics facilitates a deeper understanding of consumer
behavior, preferences, and needs. This understanding is crucial for creating personalized marketing campaigns that resonate with individual consumers. For instance, in the energy industry, big data analysis has been instrumental in transforming and upgrading marketing strategies, enabling power enterprises to offer value-added services through personalized and
differentiated services (Wang et al., 2022). Moreover, the interrelationship between big data, marketing analytics, and firm marketing capabilities has become a focal point of research. Studies have shown that the use of big data positively influences the use of marketing analytics, which in turn enhances various aspects of firm marketing capabilities, including planning, implementation, brand management, customer
relationship management, and product development (Cao, Tian, & Blankson, 2022). This synergy underscores the critical role of big data in enhancing a firm's competitive advantage in the market.


