Overview of the Growing Importance of Big Data in the Marketing Landscape.
The integration of big data into the marketing landscape marks a significant shift in how businesses approach consumer engagement and strategy development. This paper provides an overview of the growing importance of big data in marketing, highlighting its transformative
impact on decision-making processes, customer-centricity, and competitive advantage. The digital age has ushered in an era where consumers increasingly engage through digital channels, generating vast amounts of data. This data, when harnessed effectively, enables businesses to uncover unmet consumer demands and expectations, thereby achieving
sustainable business success (Cavlak & Cop, 2021). The role of big data in digital marketing extends beyond mere data collection; it involves the strategic analysis and application of this data to drive marketing decisions and long-term business strategies (Rathi & Betala, 2019). Big data's significance in marketing decisions cannot be overstated. It provides companies with
the necessary insights to cater to larger markets and secure a competitive edge. The challenge lies in sifting through the vast data to extract meaningful information that can inform strategic decisions (Rathi & Betala, 2019). This process of data management and analysis is crucial in framing both long-term strategies and short-term tactics, ultimately contributing to a sustainable
competitive advantage. Furthermore, the importance of big data extends to customer-centric marketing. In today's digital and mobile-driven market, real-time, personalized marketing has become more prevalent than ever. Businesses increasingly rely on digital media and mobile technologies to create
targeted customer experiences. Big data analytics plays a pivotal role in this context, driving consumer insights and engagement, and improving organizational performance (Camilleri, 2016). The application of big data in business extends to various sectors, including social media.
Companies worldwide are leveraging big data analytics to process heterogeneous data types from social media, aiming to improve performance and increase revenue. This trend underscores the capability of big data to guide a revolutionary transformation in research, invention, and business marketing (Alsghaier, Akour, Shehabat, & Aldiabat, 2017). In conclusion, the growing importance of big data in the marketing landscape is evident in its
ability to enhance decision-making, foster customer-centricity, and secure a competitive advantage. As businesses continue to navigate the digital age, the strategic application of big


