LITERATURE REVIEW
Big Data in Marketing
The application of big data in marketing represents a significant shift in how businesses approach market analysis, consumer engagement, and strategy development. This literature review explores the existing body of work on the application of big data in marketing,
highlighting key findings, methodologies, and implications for the field.
Technological Advancements and Marketing Strategies:
Technological advancements have enabled marketers to access extensive information about consumers through digital channels. Big data analytics allows businesses to understand unmet
consumer demands and expectations, leading to sustainable business success (Cavlak & Cop, 2021). The integration of big data in digital marketing environments has revolutionized traditional marketing approaches, providing deeper insights into consumer behavior and preferences.
Big Data Analytics in Marketing:
Big data analytics plays a crucial role in marketing by providing accurate and comprehensive market insights. It helps enterprises understand consumer needs and market trends, thereby enabling the development of personalized and accurate marketing strategies (Liu, Wan, & Yu,
2023). The impact of big data analysis on marketing strategy is primarily reflected in the improvement of consumer insight, the accuracy of target market positioning, and the implementation of personalized marketing.
Marketing Analytics and Big Data:
The use of big data in marketing analytics involves balancing analytics to identify opportunities for improvement based on past and present data to predict and influence future trends (Goi, n.d.). This approach requires a systematic analysis of literature reviews and empirical research to understand the potential value and actual effect of big data analysis on marketing decisions.
Big Data in Retail Marketing:
In the context of retail marketing, big data has driven digital transformation by providing faster insights from data. The increasing speed of data generation has posed challenges for organizations in extracting useful data for decision-making. Big data-driven decisions help organizations address industry challenges and make informed decisions based on valuable data
(Aqif, n.d.). The review addresses definitions, types of big data, different techniques, and methods used to extract customer and business information from big data, highlighting the key benefits of big data in retail marketing.


