Exploration of Existing Literature on the Application of Big Data in Marketing.
The integration of big data into marketing strategies has become a pivotal aspect of modern business practices. This literature review explores the application of big data in marketing, focusing on its impact, methodologies, and the challenges faced in its implementation.
Understanding Big Data and Marketing Analytics:
The convergence of big data analytics (BDA) and marketing analytics (MA) has led to the development of new strategies, metrics, and concepts in digital marketing. Lacarcel, PolancoDiges, and Debasa (n.d.) conducted a systematic literature review to identify and categorize key concepts related to BDA and MA. They found 13 key concepts each for BDA and MA, which were classified according to their application in technologies or actions in digital marketing.
This study highlights the growing complexity and sophistication of marketing strategies in the era of big data.
Impact of Big Data on Marketing Strategy:
Liu, Wan, and Yu (2023) explored the application and impact of big data analysis on marketing
strategies. Their study revealed that big data analysis provides accurate and comprehensive market insights, enabling enterprises to better understand consumer needs and market trends. This leads to the development of personalized and accurate marketing strategies. The study emphasizes the importance of strengthening data collection and integration, establishing a data
analysis team, and utilizing various analysis techniques for effective marketing.
Digital Transformation in Marketing:
Miklošík and Evans (2020) discussed the impact of big data and machine learning on the digital transformation of the marketing industry. Their research identified gaps in existing research and
