Advances in Personalized Marketing Techniques
The evolution of personalized marketing techniques has been significantly influenced by advancements in technology, particularly in the realms of big data and artificial intelligence
(AI). This literature review explores recent developments in personalized marketing, examining how these technologies are reshaping marketing strategies and consumer engagement.
Perception of Personalized Marketing:
Kerem and Ulla (2018) investigated how consumers perceive the use of their personal data for
customized marketing messages and product offers. Their qualitative study among Estonian consumers revealed a generally positive attitude towards data-based personalization, provided consumers perceive benefits from disclosing their data. This study highlights the importance of balancing the perceived intrusiveness of personalized marketing with the perceived benefits to
the consumer.
AI in Precision Marketing:
El Koufi and Belangour (2023) conducted a survey on the current trends of AI applications in precision marketing. Their study reviewed various AI approaches applied to precision marketing, including machine learning, data mining, and recommendation systems. The
findings suggest that methods like Random Forest (RF), Support Vector Machine (SVM), Neural Networks (NN), and collaborative filtering provide better results in precision marketing. This study underscores the potential of AI techniques in enhancing personalized communication between customers and companies.
Big Data in Consumer Behavior Analysis:
Zhao (2023) analyzed consumer behavior in the era of big data and explored personalized marketing strategies. The study found that utilizing big data significantly enhances the effectiveness of marketing strategies, leading to increased customer satisfaction and loyalty.
This research discusses the challenges and opportunities of big data in consumer behavior analysis and presents case studies illustrating effective personalized marketing approaches.
Real-Time Personalization Techniques:
Gounaris, Skoularidou, and Tzelepis (n.d.) introduced a real-time mechanism for targeted
dynamic personalization in electronic retailing. This mechanism, a set of software components, can be integrated into existing e-commerce systems to provide personalized services such as targeted advertisements and narrowcasting promotion techniques. The study emphasizes the strategic role of the consumer in the Internet economy and how marketers can utilize technology
to target customers more personally and effectively. In conclusion, Advances in personalized marketing techniques, driven by big data and AI, are transforming the marketing landscape. These technologies enable marketers to understand consumer preferences more deeply and tailor their strategies accordingly. As personalized
marketing continues to evolve, it is crucial for businesses to understand and leverage these advancements to enhance consumer engagement and achieve marketing success.
